![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Initializing `self.urls` in `__init__` is highly recommended to prevent a potential `AttributeError` if `get_tool_session` is called before `add_tool_server` has run or if `add_tool_server` fails early. This ensures that the `urls` attribute is always defined on the instance.

```suggestion
    def __init__(self):
        self.harmony_tool_descriptions = {}
        self.urls: dict[str, str] = {}
```

